*> Scalar codecs of docs/protocol/00-data-types.md §2 to §6 (contracts/proto-api.md §2 "Scalars").
*> Every PB-PUT-x appends to the PB-BUFFER passed first; every PB-GET-x reads at PB-POS. A short or
*> malformed read sets PB-ERROR, leaves PB-POS where it was before the call and yields 0 / empty.
*> A value a writer cannot encode (over-long string, invalid identifier, bit outside a fixed set)
*> sets PB-ERROR and appends nothing. Wire numbers are big-endian (00 §1); BINARY-* items are native
*> little-endian, so fixed-width values go through a REDEFINES and FUNCTION REVERSE (research R2).

