 PROGRAM-ID. PB-GET-BE-INTEGER.
*> USING PB-BUFFER, width (BINARY-LONG 1 to 8), signed (BINARY-LONG 1 = two's complement),
*> value out (BINARY-DOUBLE).
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-BE                  PIC X(8).
 01 WS-LE                  PIC X(8).
 01 WS-UNSIGNED REDEFINES WS-LE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
 01 WS-SIGNED REDEFINES WS-LE BINARY-DOUBLE SIGNED.
 01 WS-HALF                PIC 9(20).
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 L-WIDTH                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-SIGNED               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-VALUE                BINARY-DOUBLE.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING PB-BUFFER L-WIDTH L-SIGNED L-VALUE.
     MOVE LOW-VALUES TO WS-BE
     CALL "PB-GET-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BE(9 - L-WIDTH:L-WIDTH) L-WIDTH
     MOVE FUNCTION REVERSE(WS-BE) TO WS-LE
     COMPUTE WS-HALF = 2 ** (8 * L-WIDTH - 1)
     EVALUATE TRUE
         WHEN L-WIDTH = 8
             MOVE WS-SIGNED TO L-VALUE
         WHEN L-SIGNED = 1 AND WS-UNSIGNED >= WS-HALF
             COMPUTE L-VALUE = WS-UNSIGNED - 2 * WS-HALF
         WHEN OTHER
             MOVE WS-UNSIGNED TO L-VALUE
     END-EVALUATE
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM PB-GET-BE-INTEGER.

